Subject: [PATCH] bpf: add Mihomo packet-rewrite prerequisites to Lineage 4.9

Base: LineageOS/android_kernel_oneplus_sdm845 228c16bfcd256a546e3fde375215f6072135588f
Donor: Linux v4.19.325 a67e7cdde7cc7984ae24c3c81a70dc1aa34424b1
Source: https://github.com/gregkh/linux/tree/v4.19.325
Privileged verifier work budget: Linux 5.2 c04c0d2b968ac45d6ef020316808ef6c82325a82

Backport LRU/LPM maps, scalar tracking, BPF subprogram verification/execution,
program/map information and ARM64 JIT support. Adapt the existing 4.9 context,
helper, cgroup, perf and VFS interfaces; keep unsupported hooks unregistered.
Sync the classic BPF converter and UDP checksum enforcement from the donor.
Use a 1M privileged verifier work budget; retain the old unprivileged budget
and 4096-slot program-size limit. Add only the skb test-run execution path,
with bounded output and a copy of the actual input size before alignment.
Retain original licensing and copyright notices in imported files.

Experimental; see docs/mihomo-ebpf-backport.md for scope and validation.

